ntions version control for prompts. It stays vague where the question asks for a specific approach.\"}","toolUses":[],"stopReason":"end_turn","usage":{"input":435,"output":313,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0},"model":"claude-haiku-5-5"},"costUsd":0.0002,"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","ts":1793427003389},"8a5e996fed95912a13bda0315b920917bd57e7242c930c490fc4a4197395a908":{"response":{"text":"","toolUses":[{"id":"toolu_01YS8Y7xnjH4YFHybtGwe1Av","name":"save_memory","input":{"reason":"Recording what worked this run so the next Data Engineer (mid) search starts from the right candidate pool and evidence patterns.","role":"data-engineering","note":"Data Engineer (mid) run, 21 tool calls, 0 reformulations. Semantic search on \"PySpark/Databricks batch pipelines\" gave a strong pool. Five candidates reached full must-have evidence: c030, c051, c171, c118, c041. Evidence patterns: PySpark/Databricks jobs support Spark and pipelines; dbt/Snowflake modelling supports SQL; \"DAG orchestration\" supports Airflow only loosely (c030 Airflow citation was rejected, c051/c171/c041 accepted it as implied); Kafka consumers support streaming. Two SQL citations were rejected as non-verbatim, and retrying with a different verbatim sentence worked for both. Assessment grades: c030 0.92, c051 0.92, c171 0.90, c118 0.65 (sandbox code 2/3), c041 0.55 (sandbox code 1/3). Fairness audit: rho=1, top-5 overlap 100%, no blind ranking needed. Dropped nothing.","preferred_skills":["Spark / PySpark","SQL and dbt modelling","data pipelines / DAG orchestration","Airflow","Kafka / streaming"]}}],"stopReason":"tool_use","usage":{"input":37155,"output":627,"cacheRead":2519,"cacheWrite":0},"model":"claude-haiku-5-5"},"costUsd":0.00405419,"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","ts":1793427003987},"55d55dbc884c2512776d3669c14b662e374f1eedd4cf4196acc78d9fb8c9e578":{"response":{"text":"","toolUses":[{"id":"toolu_01FYRoF6SjSeRS1Kf1sZ4CSK","name":"advance_phase","input":{"reason":"The fairness audit ran on the live shortlist (rho=