ncise.\"}","toolUses":[],"stopReason":"end_turn","usage":{"input":563,"output":132,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0},"model":"claude-haiku-5-5"},"costUsd":0.00012230000000000002,"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","ts":1793427008203},"0f7a7ff3b4a8839e831eaa4bb65a9220d41ca3c189329598e38063454729fed9":{"response":{"text":"","toolUses":[{"id":"toolu_01NseMWy6u6pAzFARao1vfoy","name":"finalize_shortlist","input":{"reason":"All five approved candidates have verbatim evidence for all three must-haves and the fairness audit found no identity effect (rho=1, top-5 overlap 100%), so the blind ranking is not needed and the scored order stands.","ranked_ids":["c030","c051","c171","c118","c041"],"weights":{"semantic":0.6,"assessment":0.4},"official_blind":false,"summary":"Data Engineer (mid) shortlist of five, ranked by 0.6 × semantic + 0.4 × assessment. 1. c030 Sam Nair: 0.854 (sem 0.81, grade 0.92). 2. c051 Manish Petrov: 0.830 (sem 0.77, grade 0.92). 3. c171 Elias Nair: 0.792 (sem 0.72, grade 0.90). 4. c118 Pranav Saxena: 0.674 (sem 0.69, grade 0.65; sandbox code 2/3). 5. c041 Aditya Fischer: 0.658 (sem 0.73, grade 0.55; sandbox code 1/3). All five have verbatim evidence for Spark, SQL and data pipelines. Airflow is evidenced only as DAG orchestration, and only for c051, c171 and c041; c030's Airflow citation was rejected and c118's was not established. Streaming is evidenced for all five through Kafka consumers. Tool calls: 23 of 25 used. Reformulations: 0 of 2 used, with one semantic search plus profile opens and citations. Dropped: none of the approved candidates; non-evidenced pool members (c177, Dev Garcia, Aditya Kulkarni, c016, Manish Joshi, c135, Aditya Garcia) were never shortlisted because they had no must-have evidence. Two SQL quotes were rejected as non-verbatim and replaced successfully. Fairness audit: rho=1, top-5 overlap 100%, no identity-driven movement, so blind ranking is not official."}}],"stopReason":"tool_use","usage":{"input":39946,"output":1100,"cacheRead":2109,"ca