r every piece."},{"requirement_id":"n2","quote":"Brought Largest Contentful Paint under 1.5s on the marketing site by code-splitting and image work."}]}}],"stopReason":"tool_use","usage":{"input":22848,"output":570,"cacheRead":3220,"cacheWrite":0},"model":"claude-haiku-5-5"},"costUsd":0.002602,"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","ts":1793427276248},"5cfe3765e0360967f17e284f38a9749e0ad4b101783564d19d33377d1d881e9b":{"response":{"text":"{\"label\":\"yes\",\"confidence\":0.9,\"rationale\":\"Next.js is a React framework, so building Next.js UIs implies hands-on React work. The sentence also cites Preact, which is React-compatible, and concrete Core Web Vitals work (LCP, CLS), which shows shipped front-end work rather than a bare keyword.\"}","toolUses":[],"stopReason":"end_turn","usage":{"input":338,"output":258,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0},"model":"claude-haiku-5-5"},"costUsd":0.0001628,"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","ts":1793427278270},"0e67af506ba89de279bb9d3943661bf4860d84b3b2b30dffd1153feeebd997ab":{"response":{"text":"Four candidates are now fully evidenced on both must-haves, and the llm-apps pool looks exhausted. I'll request approval with these four.","toolUses":[{"id":"toolu_013DagyEW9ywkFUEnpENQ194","name":"request_hr_approval","input":{"reason":"Four candidates have verbatim evidence for both must-haves (LLM applications, evaluation). The llm-apps pool appears exhausted: the remaining candidates are unrelated backgrounds, and the other llm-apps profiles were keyword-only and dropped. Requesting approval at 4 of target 5.","candidate_ids":["c100","c162","c077","c020"],"rationale":"Shortlist (all four have verbatim citations for m1 and m2; nice-to-haves cited where available):\n- c100 Ravi Bose (4y): shipped grounded chat assistants end to end with a graded held-out set gating releases; regressions tracked per release. Nice: RAG (rejected by local check, cosine 0.35), agents (partial).\n- c162 Kunal Joshi (5y): built a grounded chat assistant with citation spans checked against sources; graded outputs with held-out set and regression tracking. Nice: RAG, agents (partial).\n- c077 Ivan Petrov (5y): shipped grounded chat assistants with graded held-out set gating every release; RAG and agents (partial).\n- c020 Nora Sharma (6y): shipped grounded chat assistants end to end with held-out set gating releases; rubric grading with regression tracking. Nice: RAG, agents (partial).\nDropped during sourcing (keyword-only, no project evidence for must-haves): Ravi Sharma (c060), Maya Mukherjee (c129), Rahul Bose (c131). Shortlist is 4 of target 5; no fifth fully evidenced candidate found in the pool."}}],"stopReason":"tool_use","usage":{"input":41633,"output":817,"cacheRead":3220,"cacheWrite":0},"model":"claude-haiku-5-5"},"costUsd":0.004604,"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","ts":1793427278582},"87cbbac5910c1a126f1a54cdf313f5756e9a1b1b9ef410f523e3f0ff8b6a9e39":{"response":{"text":"{\"parts\":[{\"kind\":\"short\",\"score\":0.9,\"confidence\":0.8,\"note\":\"Covers a concrete POST body with query, limit, opaque keyset cursor, and filters; validates against an allowlist with 422 errors; and uses additive changes or a new version path.\"},{\"kind\":\"scenario\",\"score\":0.9,\"confidence\":0.8,\"note\":\"Keeps the old field during a deprecation window, adds the new score under a distinct name with a capability flag, tracks per-client usage, and removes the old behavior only after usage hits zero or a cutoff.\"},{\"kind\":\"code\",\"score\":0.8,\"confidence\":0.45,\"note\":\"The code parses with JSON.parse, filters for both 'public' and 'indexed', preserves order, and returns JSON.stringify, which yields '[]' on no match. No hidden-test result was supplied, so the score rests on code inspection alone.\"}]}","toolUses":[],"stopReason":"end_turn","usage":{"input":1523,"output":724,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0},"model":"claude-haiku-5-5"},"costUsd":0.0005143,"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","ts":1793427279568},"2ef9a617d65fa387bf170c531110cc686686fc807f99d60324a749